    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look poised for a high-ceiling outing today, led by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest efficiency score (83.29) as he prepares to face the vulnerable Alcantara. His elite standing is bolstered by a significant dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching, making him our primary engine for Runs and RBI. Similarly, **Josh Lowe** (69.20) and **Nolan Schanuel** (67.16) provide excellent depth against the struggling Fedde; **Josh Lowe** remains a critical component of our strategy given the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher, which significantly inflates his stolen base probability despite his low spot in the batting order. We are also capitalizing on **Josh Jung**'s favorable matchup against the high xERA of Rodr\u00edguez (7.06), as the combination of a weak opposing arm and neutral platoon usage creates a high-floor outcome.\n\nThe decision to bench **Marcell Ozuna** (62.50) was the most difficult call of the morning. While he carries a strong score, he fell just short of the efficiency thresholds maintained by the likes of **Heliot Ramos** and **Kyle Tucker**, who offer superior defensive-situational versatility today. **Heliot Ramos** in particular stands out; his projection is boosted by a slow delivery from the opposing starter, offering a sneaky opportunity to steal a base in a category where we remain hyper-aggressive. While we feel confident in the starting nine, we are keeping a close eye on the weather and the confirmed batting order for **Drake Baldwin** and **Jacob Wilson**; both are currently reliant on their leadoff spots to maintain their efficiency ratings, and any shift down the lineup could trigger a re-evaluation of their utility against tough arms like Kirby and S\u00e1nchez.",
